#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# sow

#% text
# `sow(e)` gives `e` and hands it to the innermost enclosing `reap`. `sow(e, tag)` gives it a tag (a list of tags: once per tag); a `reap` whose pattern does not match the tag passes it on to an outer one. Outside any `reap` it only gives `e`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
reap({ sow(1); sow(2); 3 })
#% output
#= [3, [[1, 2]]]

#% cell
reap({ sow(1, odd); sow(2, even); sow(3, odd) }, odd)
#% output
#= [3, [[1, 3]]]

#% cell
sow(5)
#% output
#= 5

